67.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَغْرِبَ\",\"after\":\"The sun’s eye reaches its setting place. The distant sunset becomes the visible passage of the solar disk toward the horizon.\",\"reason\":\"The rare عَيْنٍ sense is the sun’s round disk, while مَغْرِبَ names the sun’s setting place. The disk and its destination join in one image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N167.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلشَّمْسِ\",\"after\":\"The rare “eye of the sun” sense names the same sun that appears in the phrase. The wording lets its disk-like eye echo the celestial body already on the scene.\",\"reason\":\"عَيْنٍ can mean عين الشمس, the sun’s disk; ٱلشَّمْسِ names the sun itself. These senses meet in the same referent, with the rare branch sharpening its round visible form.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N167.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَغْرُبُ\",\"after\":\"What is setting is heard as the solar disk itself. The verb’s subject becomes a visible round orb descending from view.\",\"reason\":\"عَيْنٍ has the sense of the sun’s disk, while تَغْرُبُ means to set or disappear below the horizon. The orb and its motion form an actor-and-action pair.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N168\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N168.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَمِئَةٍ\",\"after\":\"The dark mud seems to fill an eye-like hollow. The sun’s setting is pictured in a notch or bowl made heavy with silt.\",\"reason\":\"عَيْنٍ can name a hollow or depression, as in a notch of a well or knee; حَمِئَةٍ names black muddy water. The hollow gives the mud a shape and makes the setting a single dark-filled image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N169\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N170\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N171\",\"lines\":\"----n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N171.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"عَيْنٍ\